From 04ef968cfda88fd0c0f73131b8461ed753b33e0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:05:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(tools)!: a tool's library holder is a reference to
 the entry

A tool that sits in a built-in library holder stores the entry's name,
the gauge length and the projection (HolderRef on ToolBody::library),
not a drawn copy of the outline. tool_body::build_library is the one
place a reference becomes a shape: the SetToolBody / AddTool command,
the project loader and the .camtools reader call it, so the collision
laws, the stamp, the simulation and the preview read one body.

- Project (v62) and .camtools (version 2 when a tool names a library
  holder) write `holder: {entry, gauge_len, projection}` in place of
  `body`.
- An older file is not rewritten: a drawn copy of a library holder and
  a holder_d/holder_len cylinder load as the custom holder they were.
- A name the library does not hold, a grouped pick, lengths the entry
  cannot take, or `holder` beside `body` refuse the file by tool name.
- MCP set_tool_holder writes the reference (holder.library in get_job);
  add_tool refuses a definition's own holder reference, edit_tool a
  holder patch.
- UI: the tool settings show the entry's holder diameter and length as
  text; the Profile tab names the entry and the picker shows it. The
  unchanged outline keeps the reference, an edited point makes the
  holder a custom profile.

Pinned for every library entry: judged tool, envelope, band stack,
stamp term and facets equal those of the drawn copy an older build
stored (crates/app/tests/holder_reference.rs).

Stacked on #2054.

BREAKING CHANGE: a project or tool library saved with a library holder
states it as a reference (project v62, .camtools version 2); v0.21.0 and
older refuse such a file. `ToolBody` has a new public field `library`.

Fixes #2016

